WEBVTT

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.588
Read these two phrases: the river bank;

00:00:03.608 --> 00:00:05.211
the bank refused the loan.

00:00:05.386 --> 00:00:07.556
The letters in bank are identical.

00:00:07.732 --> 00:00:09.683
Should its vector be identical too?

00:00:09.845 --> 00:00:12.093
If the vector is just a stored address for

00:00:12.113 --> 00:00:14.297
a word, how could the surrounding sentence

00:00:14.317 --> 00:00:15.082
change it?

00:00:17.503 --> 00:00:19.254
That is the difference between a classic

00:00:19.274 --> 00:00:22.128
static word vector and a contextual token

00:00:22.148 --> 00:00:23.210
representation.

00:00:23.385 --> 00:00:25.942
One reuses a stored vector for the string.

00:00:26.117 --> 00:00:28.623
The other computes a representation for

00:00:28.643 --> 00:00:30.491
this occurrence from its sequence.

00:00:31.387 --> 00:00:33.596
Classic word two vec gives bank

00:00:33.616 --> 00:00:36.186
essentially the same stored vector in both

00:00:36.206 --> 00:00:39.266
sentences. A contextual encoder starts

00:00:39.286 --> 00:00:42.114
with token embeddings and transforms them

00:00:42.134 --> 00:00:43.930
using the surrounding sequence.

00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:45.980
River supplies different evidence from

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.887
refused and loan.

00:00:48.470 --> 00:00:50.871
Our two moving markers illustrate that

00:00:50.891 --> 00:00:52.933
distinction; their coordinates are

00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:55.188
invented. They do not measure a model's

00:00:55.208 --> 00:00:57.701
ability to disambiguate bank, and

00:00:57.721 --> 00:00:59.363
different vectors alone would not

00:00:59.383 --> 00:01:02.018
establish that a model interpreted the two

00:01:02.038 --> 00:01:03.409
sentences correctly.

00:01:04.322 --> 00:01:06.233
A Transformer's self-attention lets a

00:01:06.253 --> 00:01:09.467
token's representation draw on information

00:01:09.487 --> 00:01:11.645
from other tokens in the sequence.

00:01:11.807 --> 00:01:13.746
It is a mechanism for combining

00:01:13.766 --> 00:01:16.503
information. What the model learns to do

00:01:16.523 --> 00:01:18.282
with that mechanism depends on its

00:01:18.302 --> 00:01:19.093
training.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.351
Contextual representations did not begin

00:01:22.371 --> 00:01:23.678
with Transformers.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.856
ELMo used bidirectional recurrent

00:01:25.876 --> 00:01:28.563
networks. Transformer encoders later

00:01:28.583 --> 00:01:31.269
became dominant as self-attention helped

00:01:31.289 --> 00:01:34.233
make large-scale sequence processing more

00:01:34.253 --> 00:01:35.366
parallelisable.

00:01:35.541 --> 00:01:38.472
Architecture and training objective remain

00:01:38.492 --> 00:01:39.812
separate choices.

00:01:40.707 --> 00:01:43.046
There is another trap: the units a model

00:01:43.066 --> 00:01:45.817
receives are not necessarily the terms an

00:01:45.837 --> 00:01:47.466
inverted index stores.

00:01:47.654 --> 00:01:50.508
For this illustration only, define a toy

00:01:50.528 --> 00:01:53.407
tokenizer that makes one character per

00:01:53.427 --> 00:01:56.912
token. Jobs becomes four units: j, o, b,

00:01:56.932 --> 00:01:57.723
s.

00:01:58.288 --> 00:02:00.682
A separate illustrative lexical analyser

00:02:00.702 --> 00:02:03.981
lowercases jobs and stems it to job.

00:02:04.156 --> 00:02:06.327
Those are different representations made

00:02:06.347 --> 00:02:07.744
for different jobs.

00:02:07.906 --> 00:02:11.159
Real neural tokenizers may use subwords,

00:02:11.282 --> 00:02:13.143
characters or bytes.

00:02:13.318 --> 00:02:16.327
Our character split does not claim how any

00:02:16.347 --> 00:02:18.903
named model tokenizes this word.

00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:22.840
Contextual token representations are still

00:02:22.860 --> 00:02:25.920
several vectors, one for each token

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.561
occurrence. A model producing a single

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:31.448
embedding for a complete query or passage

00:02:31.468 --> 00:02:32.736
needs another step.

00:02:32.924 --> 00:02:36.151
Pooling can combine token representations,

00:02:36.313 --> 00:02:38.059
or the model can use a selected

00:02:38.079 --> 00:02:39.192
representation.

00:02:39.763 --> 00:02:42.063
Our declared toy averages three two-number

00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:46.509
vectors: one, three; three, one; and two,

00:02:46.529 --> 00:02:49.085
two. The result is two, two.

00:02:49.261 --> 00:02:51.895
This demonstrates mean pooling only.

00:02:52.044 --> 00:02:54.009
It is not a claim about BERT's default

00:02:54.029 --> 00:02:56.354
retrieval behavior or the best pooling

00:02:56.374 --> 00:02:57.023
method.

00:02:57.944 --> 00:03:00.191
An encoder computes an output using a

00:03:00.211 --> 00:03:01.234
fitted mapping.

00:03:01.409 --> 00:03:03.851
With the same model, preprocessing and

00:03:03.871 --> 00:03:06.273
inference settings, its output can be

00:03:06.293 --> 00:03:08.992
reproduced. Training is the stage that

00:03:09.012 --> 00:03:11.660
changes the mapping; applying it need not

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:12.999
train the model again.

00:03:13.564 --> 00:03:16.022
Reproducibility is different from

00:03:16.042 --> 00:03:17.310
interpretability.

00:03:17.485 --> 00:03:19.978
Individual dimensions usually do not

00:03:19.998 --> 00:03:22.929
arrive with labels such as occupation or

00:03:22.949 --> 00:03:25.803
emotion. Our two-number diagrams make

00:03:25.823 --> 00:03:28.818
operations visible; real representations

00:03:28.838 --> 00:03:31.898
distribute patterns across many dimensions

00:03:31.918 --> 00:03:34.526
and cannot be inspected as a simple map.

00:03:35.416 --> 00:03:37.730
Now return to the two uses of bank.

00:03:37.906 --> 00:03:40.398
Context can change the representation.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.177
Pooling can make one vector for the

00:03:42.197 --> 00:03:45.746
complete text. Neither step, by itself,

00:03:45.908 --> 00:03:48.143
establishes that independently encoded

00:03:48.163 --> 00:03:50.373
questions will rank close to the passages

00:03:50.393 --> 00:03:51.571
a searcher needs.

00:03:52.124 --> 00:03:54.270
That relationship depends on architecture

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:56.615
and training, and its usefulness needs

00:03:56.635 --> 00:03:59.167
evaluation. Before accepting a claim about

00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:02.027
contextual embeddings, ask what text unit

00:04:02.047 --> 00:04:04.476
the vector represents, how that vector was

00:04:04.496 --> 00:04:07.027
obtained, and what task taught the model

00:04:07.047 --> 00:04:08.908
which relationships to reward.
